# Libraries Ferry, freemac's runner for Mac apps, loads when a Mac app needs
# them: libc++ for apps written in C++, 7-Zip to open disk images (.dmg) and
# libcurl for networking, libturbojpeg for cameras that send Motion JPEG,
# and clang and lld, which build a Metal app's shaders when it runs
# (freemac 1.262). FluidSynth and its General MIDI sound bank play MIDI
# for apps that use Core Audio's synthesizers (VLC's .mid files, freemac
# 1.264). Core Audio's AAC and other sound encoders use the system's FFmpeg
# (libavcodec), which the desktop's gstreamer1.0-libav already brings.
# Installed with Ferry's own package (FERRY_DEB);
# Ferry carries on without any of them, so a missing one only turns off what
# it does.
libc++1
libc++abi1
7zip
libcurl4t64
libturbojpeg
clang
lld
libfluidsynth3
fluid-soundfont-gm
